🏨 Hostel Complaint Management System (Backend)

A role-based complaint management backend system built using Spring Boot, JWT Authentication, MySQL, and JPA.
Designed to handle complaint lifecycle management within a hostel environment with strict role-based access control.

🚀 Features
🔐 Authentication & Authorization

JWT-based authentication

Role-based access control (RBAC)

Secure endpoints using Spring Security

👥 Supported Roles

STUDENT

WORKER

CARETAKER

WARDEN

MESS_CONVENOR

📝 Complaint Lifecycle

A complaint follows this structured flow:

CREATED → ASSIGNED → IN_PROGRESS → RESOLVED → CLOSED / REJECTED

Students create complaints

Caretaker/Warden assigns worker

Worker updates progress & uploads proof

Student closes complaint after resolution

📊 Core Functionalities

Create complaint (Student only)

Assign worker (Caretaker/Warden only)

Update complaint status (Worker only)

Close complaint (Student only)

Paginated complaint listing

Status-based filtering

Role-based data visibility

Dashboard analytics (counts by status)

Notification system

🏗️ Tech Stack

Java 17+

Spring Boot

Spring Security

JWT (io.jsonwebtoken)

Spring Data JPA (Hibernate)

MySQL

Maven

Lombok

📂 Project Architecture
Controller → Service → Repository → Database

Controller Layer – Handles REST APIs

Service Layer – Business logic & role validation

Repository Layer – Database interaction using JPA

Entity Layer – Mapped relational models

DTO Layer – Clean request/response separation

Security Layer – JWT filter + SecurityConfig

🗄️ Database Design Highlights
User Entity

Unique email

Role-based fields

Scholar number unique for students

Many-to-One relationship with complaints

Complaint Entity

Many-to-One: Student

Many-to-One: Assigned Worker

Enum-based status, category & priority

Auto-managed timestamps

 API Endpoints

Authentication
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/auth/register	Register new user
POST	/api/auth/login	Login & receive JWT

Complaint APIs
Method	Endpoint	Access
POST	/api/complaints	STUDENT
PUT	/api/complaints/{id}/assign	CARETAKER / WARDEN
PUT	/api/complaints/{id}/status	WORKER
PUT	/api/complaints/{id}/close	STUDENT
GET	/api/complaints	Role-based
GET	/api/complaints/dashboard	CARETAKER / WARDEN

Security Implementation

Stateless authentication

Custom JWT filter

Bearer token validation

Role extraction from token

Method-level security restrictions

Endpoint-based access control

Role-Based Logic Examples

Only STUDENT can create complaints

Only CARETAKER/WARDEN can assign workers

Only assigned WORKER can update status

Only complaint owner (STUDENT) can close complaint

Complaint must be RESOLVED before closing